<tool id="kleborate" name="Kleborate" version="@TOOL_VERSION@+galaxy@VERSION_SUFFIX@" profile="@PROFILE@">
    <description>screen genome assemblies of Klebsiella and Escherichia</description>
    <macros>
        <token name="@TOOL_VERSION@">3.3.0b1</token>
        <token name="@VERSION_SUFFIX@">0</token>
        <token name="@PROFILE@">25.1</token>
        <xml name="species_thresholds">
            <section name="advanced" title="Advanced options" expanded="false">
                <param argument="--general__species_strong" type="float" min="0" max="1" value="0.02" label="Mash distance threshold for a strong species match"/>
                <param argument="--general__species_weak" type="float" min="0" max="1" value="0.04" label="Mash distance threshold for a weak species match"/>
                <param argument="--trim_headers" type="boolean" truevalue="--trim_headers" falsevalue="" checked="true" label="Trim module names from column headers?" help="If disabled, every column of the full results table is prefixed with its module name (e.g. kpsc__mlst__ST)"/>
            </section>
        </xml>
    </macros>
    <xrefs>
        <xref type="bio.tools">kleborate</xref>
    </xrefs>
    <requirements>
        <requirement type="package" version="@TOOL_VERSION@">kleborate</requirement>
    </requirements>
    <version_command>kleborate --version</version_command>
    <command detect_errors="aggressive"><![CDATA[
#import re

mkdir input &&
## Symlink input files for human-readable strain names in the output tables
#set $inputs = []
#for $a in $assemblies
    #set $name = re.sub(r'[^\w\-.]', '_', str($a.element_identifier))
    ln -s '$a' 'input/$name' &&
    #silent $inputs.append('input/' + $name)
#end for

kleborate
    -t "\${GALAXY_SLOTS:-1}"
    -o out
    $sc.advanced.trim_headers
    -m 'general__species${',' + str($sc.modules) if $sc.modules else ''}'
    #if $sc.type == 'kpsc'
        --kpsc__amr_min_identity $sc.amr.kpsc__amr_min_identity
        --kpsc__amr_min_coverage $sc.amr.kpsc__amr_min_coverage
        --kpsc__amr_min_spurious_identity $sc.amr.kpsc__amr_min_spurious_identity
        --kpsc__amr_min_spurious_coverage $sc.amr.kpsc__amr_min_spurious_coverage
    #end if
    --general__species_strong $sc.advanced.general__species_strong
    --general__species_weak $sc.advanced.general__species_weak
    -a
    #for $i in $inputs
        '$i'
    #end for
    > '$concise' &&
mv out/general__species_output.txt '$results'
    ]]></command>

    <inputs>
        <param argument="--assemblies" type="data" format="fasta" multiple="true" label="FASTA file(s) of assemblies" help="You may provide multiple assemblies for screening"/>
        <conditional name="sc">
            <param name="type" type="select" label="Species complex" help="Selects which set of typing modules is available. Species detection is always run.">
                <option value="kpsc" selected="true">Klebsiella pneumoniae species complex (KpSC)</option>
                <option value="kosc">Klebsiella oxytoca species complex (KoSC)</option>
                <option value="escherichia">Escherichia coli / Shigella</option>
            </param>
            <when value="kpsc">
                <param name="modules" type="select" multiple="true" optional="true" display="checkboxes" label="Modules to run">
                    <option value="general__contig_stats" selected="true">Assembly contig statistics and QC</option>
                    <option value="kpsc__mlst" selected="true">Chromosomal MLST</option>
                    <option value="klebsiella__ybst" selected="true">Yersiniabactin (ybt) MLST</option>
                    <option value="klebsiella__cbst" selected="true">Colibactin (clb) MLST</option>
                    <option value="klebsiella__abst" selected="true">Aerobactin (iuc) MLST</option>
                    <option value="klebsiella__smst" selected="true">Salmochelin (iro) MLST</option>
                    <option value="klebsiella__rmst" selected="true">RmpADC MLST and expression status</option>
                    <option value="kpsc__virulence_score" selected="true">Virulence score</option>
                    <option value="klebsiella__rmpa2" selected="true">rmpA2 typing</option>
                    <option value="klebsiella__peg-344" selected="true">peg-344 typing</option>
                    <option value="kpsc__amr" selected="true">Acquired AMR genes and mutations</option>
                    <option value="kpsc__resistance_score" selected="true">Resistance score</option>
                    <option value="kpsc__resistance_class_count" selected="true">Resistance class count</option>
                    <option value="kpsc__resistance_gene_count" selected="true">Resistance gene count</option>
                    <option value="kpsc__cipro_prediction" selected="true">Ciprofloxacin resistance prediction</option>
                    <option value="kpsc__wzi" selected="true">wzi typing</option>
                    <option value="kpsc__kaptive" selected="true">K and O locus typing (Kaptive)</option>
                    <option value="kpsc__mrk" selected="true">mrk operon MLST</option>
                </param>
                <section name="amr" title="AMR detection thresholds" expanded="false">
                    <param argument="--kpsc__amr_min_identity" type="float" min="0" max="100" value="90" label="Minimum alignment percent identity for AMR results"/>
                    <param argument="--kpsc__amr_min_coverage" type="float" min="0" max="100" value="80" label="Minimum alignment percent coverage for AMR results"/>
                    <param argument="--kpsc__amr_min_spurious_identity" type="float" min="0" max="100" value="80" label="Minimum alignment percent identity for spurious AMR results"/>
                    <param argument="--kpsc__amr_min_spurious_coverage" type="float" min="0" max="100" value="40" label="Minimum alignment percent coverage for spurious AMR results"/>
                </section>
                <expand macro="species_thresholds"/>
            </when>
            <when value="kosc">
                <param name="modules" type="select" multiple="true" optional="true" display="checkboxes" label="Modules to run">
                    <option value="general__contig_stats" selected="true">Assembly contig statistics and QC</option>
                    <option value="kosc__mlst" selected="true">Chromosomal MLST</option>
                    <option value="klebsiella__ybst" selected="true">Yersiniabactin (ybt) MLST</option>
                    <option value="klebsiella__cbst" selected="true">Colibactin (clb) MLST</option>
                    <option value="klebsiella__abst" selected="true">Aerobactin (iuc) MLST</option>
                    <option value="klebsiella__smst" selected="true">Salmochelin (iro) MLST</option>
                    <option value="kosc__kaptive" selected="true">K and O locus typing (Kaptive)</option>
                </param>
                <expand macro="species_thresholds"/>
            </when>
            <when value="escherichia">
                <param name="modules" type="select" multiple="true" optional="true" display="checkboxes" label="Modules to run">
                    <option value="general__contig_stats" selected="true">Assembly contig statistics and QC</option>
                    <option value="escherichia__mlst_achtman" selected="true">MLST (Achtman scheme)</option>
                    <option value="escherichia__mlst_pasteur">MLST (Pasteur scheme)</option>
                    <option value="escherichia__pathovar" selected="true">Pathotype prediction</option>
                    <option value="escherichia__mlst_lee" selected="true">LEE pathogenicity island MLST</option>
                    <option value="escherichia__pks" selected="true">pks (colibactin) island detection</option>
                    <option value="escherichia__ezclermont" selected="true">Clermont phylotyping (EzClermont)</option>
                    <option value="escherichia__stxtyper" selected="true">Shiga toxin typing (StxTyper)</option>
                    <option value="escherichia__ectyper" selected="true">O/H serotyping (ECTyper)</option>
                    <option value="escherichia__kaptive" selected="true">Group 2 and 3 capsule (K) locus typing (Kaptive)</option>
                </param>
                <expand macro="species_thresholds"/>
            </when>
        </conditional>
    </inputs>

    <outputs>
        <data name="concise" format="tabular" label="${tool.name} on ${on_string}: Concise Results"/>
        <data name="results" format="tabular" label="${tool.name} on ${on_string}: Full Results"/>
    </outputs>

    <tests>
        <!-- KpSC with all default modules -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="2">
            <param name="assemblies" value="KP011_S63.scfd.fasta,KP012_S64.scfd.fasta"/>
            <conditional name="sc">
                <param name="type" value="kpsc"/>
            </conditional>
            <output name="concise" ftype="tabular" file="Kleborate_concise_results.txt" sort="true"/>
            <output name="results" ftype="tabular">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_n_lines n="3"/>
                    <has_n_columns n="135"/>
                    <has_text text="peg-344"/>
                    <has_text text="RmpADC_status"/>
                    <has_text text="mrkST"/>
                    <has_text text="ST925"/>
                    <has_text text="tet(D)"/>
                    <has_text text="KL111"/>
                    <has_text text="OL12"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <!-- KpSC with a module subset and untrimmed headers -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="2">
            <param name="assemblies" value="KP011_S63.scfd.fasta,KP012_S64.scfd.fasta"/>
            <conditional name="sc">
                <param name="type" value="kpsc"/>
                <param name="modules" value="kpsc__mlst,kpsc__wzi"/>
                <section name="advanced">
                    <param name="trim_headers" value="false"/>
                </section>
            </conditional>
            <output name="concise" ftype="tabular">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_n_lines n="3"/>
                    <has_text text="ST45-4LV"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output name="results" ftype="tabular" file="Kleborate_results_subset.txt" sort="true"/>
        </test>
        <!-- KoSC -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="2">
            <param name="assemblies" value="KP011_S63.scfd.fasta,KP012_S64.scfd.fasta"/>
            <conditional name="sc">
                <param name="type" value="kosc"/>
            </conditional>
            <output name="concise" ftype="tabular">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_n_lines n="3"/>
                    <has_text text="KP012_S64.scfd"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output name="results" ftype="tabular">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_n_lines n="3"/>
                    <has_n_columns n="78"/>
                    <has_text text="clonal_complex"/>
                    <has_text text="KL88"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <!-- Escherichia -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="2">
            <param name="assemblies" value="KP011_S63.scfd.fasta"/>
            <conditional name="sc">
                <param name="type" value="escherichia"/>
            </conditional>
            <output name="concise" ftype="tabular">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_n_lines n="2"/>
                    <has_text text="ST_Achtman"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output name="results" ftype="tabular">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_n_lines n="2"/>
                    <has_n_columns n="69"/>
                    <has_text text="Clermont_type"/>
                    <has_text text="KL180"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
    </tests>

    <help><![CDATA[
**What it does**

Kleborate screens genome assemblies of *Klebsiella pneumoniae* species complex (KpSC), *Klebsiella oxytoca* species complex (KoSC) and *Escherichia coli* / *Shigella* for:

- species (Mash-based) and assembly quality metrics
- MLST sequence types (chromosomal, and for KpSC also the *mrk* operon)
- virulence loci: yersiniabactin (ybt), colibactin (clb), aerobactin (iuc), salmochelin (iro), RmpADC (with predicted expression status), rmpA2 and peg-344
- antimicrobial resistance determinants (KpSC): acquired genes, SNPs, gene truncations, intrinsic β-lactamases and ciprofloxacin resistance prediction
- K (capsule) and O antigen (LPS) locus typing via wzi alleles and Kaptive
- for *E. coli*: Achtman/Pasteur MLST, pathotype, LEE MLST, pks island, Clermont phylotype, Shiga toxin type, O:H serotype and group 2/3 capsule loci

Choose the species complex that matches your assemblies and select the modules to run (if none are selected, only species detection is run). Species detection is always run and reported, but modules run regardless of the species detected, so check the *species* column.

More information can be found in the Kleborate documentation_.

.. _documentation: https://kleborate.readthedocs.io

**Outputs**

- Concise results: one line per assembly, with key typing results.
- Full results: one line per assembly, with all columns of the selected modules (including Kaptive K and O locus results).

**Scores**

Kleborate outputs a simple categorical virulence score and, if AMR screening is enabled, an antimicrobial resistance score (KpSC only).

The virulence score ranges from 0 to 5:

- 0 = negative for all of yersiniabactin (ybt), colibactin (clb), aerobactin (iuc)
- 1 = yersiniabactin only
- 2 = yersiniabactin and colibactin (or colibactin only)
- 3 = aerobactin (without yersiniabactin or colibactin)
- 4 = aerobactin with yersiniabactin (without colibactin)
- 5 = yersiniabactin, colibactin and aerobactin

The resistance score ranges from 0 to 3:

- 0 = no ESBL, no carbapenemase (regardless of colistin resistance)
- 1 = ESBL, no carbapenemase (regardless of colistin resistance)
- 2 = Carbapenemase without colistin resistance (regardless of ESBL genes or OmpK mutations)
- 3 = Carbapenemase with colistin resistance (regardless of ESBL genes or OmpK mutations)

**Spurious hits**

The default criteria for detection of AMR genes are minimum nucleotide identity ≥90% and coverage ≥80%. To alert users to genes that may be missed because of contig breaks or other assembly issues, Kleborate also reports 'spurious' hits that pass more relaxed criteria (default ≥80% identity, ≥40% coverage) in the *spurious_resistance_hits* column.
    ]]></help>

    <citations>
        <citation type="doi">10.1038/s41467-021-24448-3</citation> <!-- Kleborate publication -->
        <citation type="doi">10.1099/mgen.0.000102</citation><!-- Kaptive publication -->
    </citations>
</tool>
